          "filename": "Entrance to Tandragee Golf Club - geograph.org.uk - 614016.jpg",
          "caption": "Entrance to Tandragee Golf Club The Golf Club was laid out as a private course on the estate of the 9th Duke of Manchester in 1911. In 1922 the Golf Club became affiliated to the Golfing Union of Ireland. It is a picturesque 18 hole parkland golf course set in the beautiful County Armagh countryside. Parts of the course look over towards the ancient Tandragee Castle and a number of the fairways have the backdrop of the fast flowing Cusher River.",
